# Web bundling and serving

DoomPi Web builds and serves browser code only. Server facets are assembled and loaded by the client-neutral headless process.

Read [Composition and runtime bundling](../../../../docs/bundling.md) first if synchronized generations are unfamiliar.

## Build boundary

```text
doompi sync
    |
    +-- Pi extension composition
    +-- browser plugin composition
    +-- headless server facet descriptor

browser plugin composition --> DoomPi Web and the browser
server facet descriptor ----> doompi-server only
```

The browser shell ships with `@agimon-ai/doompi-web`. A synchronized browser composition contributes tabs, renderers, settings, and other UI declared by `doompiWeb.client` entries.

A package that needs host-side channels or APIs declares `doompiServer`. Those modules never enter the web bundle and DoomPi Web never imports them.

## Browser build output

For selected package roots, the web bundler validates each `doompiWeb` declaration and compiles client entries with Vite:

```text
<generation>/
  web/
  plugins/
    composition.js
    manifest.json
    assets/...
  generated/...
  pluginRoots.json
```

The output does not contain a server plugin registry, API routes, or server facets. Those artifacts belong to the headless synchronization boundary.

Browser entries may contain TypeScript, React, CSS, and Tailwind classes. Shared browser runtimes such as React, CodeMirror, the web component library, and browser security helpers are externalized so the shell supplies one compatible instance.

## Serving

The production presentation server has two responsibilities:

1. Serve the selected SPA and PWA assets.
2. Forward `/api` HTTP requests and the `/api/pi` protocol WebSocket to the configured headless endpoint.

It does not inspect session frames, retain replay state, select server modules, or authorize API requests. The headless endpoint owns those behaviors.

Use `--assets` or `DOOMPI_WEB_DIST` to select an explicit SPA directory. Use `--headless-url` and `--headless-token` to select and authenticate the upstream endpoint.

## Development

The Vite development server can generate a browser composition from `DOOMPI_WEB_PLUGIN_ROOTS` and hot reload client entries. Its `/api` proxy must point at the headless process. Changing a server facet requires rebuilding the owning package and restarting the headless process, not the web server.

## Terms

| Term                    | Meaning                                                        |
| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| DoomPi composition      | Ordered extension activation plan                              |
| Browser composition     | JavaScript and CSS generated from `doompiWeb.client` entries   |
| Server facet descriptor | Generation-pinned modules loaded by the headless process       |
| Presentation server     | Static asset server and external headless HTTP/WebSocket proxy |
